---
/*
 * /terms/ — Terms of Service.
 *
 * Terms for the open-design.ai marketing site and the local-first
 * OpenDesign software.
 */
import Layout from '../../_components/sub-page-layout.astro';

const updated = 'August 25, 2026';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Terms of Service — OpenDesign',
  url: new URL('/terms/', Astro.site).toString(),
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'OpenDesign', url: Astro.site?.toString() },
};
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — OpenDesign"
  description="The terms that govern use of the open-design.ai website and the local-first OpenDesign software."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1 class="legal-h1">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>These Terms govern your use of the website <a href="https://open-design.ai">open-design.ai</a> and the OpenDesign software provided by <strong>Powerformer, Inc.</strong> (“OpenDesign”, “we”, “us”). By using the site or software, you agree to these Terms.</p>

    <h2>1. The software is open source</h2>
    <p>The OpenDesign software is released under the <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0">Apache License 2.0</a>. Your use, modification, and distribution of the software are governed by that license. These Terms cover the website; the Apache-2.0 license controls the software itself and prevails in any conflict regarding the code.</p>

    <h2>2. Local-first BYOK</h2>
    <p>OpenDesign is local-first and BYOK (“bring your own key”): you connect your own model-provider credentials, and your use of those providers is subject to their terms and pricing. You are responsible for the keys you configure and the costs they incur. Prompts, projects, and generated artifacts stay on your machine unless you choose to share them elsewhere.</p>

    <h2>3. User content and compliance</h2>
    <p>You are responsible for prompts, files, images, code, input data, and your use of model outputs submitted through OpenDesign. You represent that you have lawful rights to process and submit that content and will not submit illegal, infringing, confidential, unauthorized, malicious, or policy-violating content.</p>
    <p>Without a separate written agreement, you must not submit specially regulated data such as health data, financial account data, identity documents, minors’ information, biometrics, precise location, full payment card data, or other sensitive personal information.</p>
    <p>You retain ownership of what you create with OpenDesign. Contributions you submit to the open-source project are licensed under the project’s license as described in its CONTRIBUTING guide.</p>

    <h2>4. Prohibited uses and high-risk contexts</h2>
    <p>You must not use OpenDesign for illegal activity, fraud, phishing, spam, malware, attacks, security bypass, privacy violations, intellectual property infringement, unlawful content generation, circumvention of model provider policies, or violations of export control or sanctions rules. Community spaces such as GitHub and Discord are also governed by their respective codes of conduct.</p>
    <p>Without OpenDesign’s written approval, OpenDesign must not be used for high-risk automated decision-making involving medical, legal, financial, employment, credit, insurance, law enforcement, critical infrastructure, or personal safety contexts.</p>

    <h2>5. Model outputs</h2>
    <p>Model outputs may be inaccurate, incomplete, or unsuitable for your purpose. You are responsible for reviewing outputs and actions taken based on them. OpenDesign does not provide medical, legal, financial, investment, or other professional advice.</p>

    <h2>6. Limits, suspension, and termination</h2>
    <p>OpenDesign may restrict access to the website or community channels for abuse, legal risk, security incidents, breach of terms, or regulatory requirements.</p>

    <h2>7. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Third-party login, analytics, hosting, and model providers are governed by their own terms and privacy policies. OpenDesign does not guarantee continuous availability of third-party services or assume responsibility beyond legal requirements for third-party model policies, pricing, latency, failures, or outputs.</p>

    <h2>8. Intellectual property and trademarks</h2>
    <p>“OpenDesign”, “Powerformer”, related logos, the website, documentation, and related intellectual property belong to Powerformer, Inc. or its licensors. Without authorization, you may not copy, modify, reverse engineer, resell, rent, or sublicense OpenDesign materials, except to the extent permitted by the Apache-2.0 license for the open-source software.</p>
    <p>Third-party names and brands referenced on the site belong to their respective owners and are used for identification only.</p>

    <h2>9. No warranty</h2>
    <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, OpenDesign is provided as-is and as-available. We do not guarantee uninterrupted, error-free service or that OpenDesign will meet every business objective.</p>

    <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Powerformer, Inc. will not be liable for indirect damages, lost profits, data loss, business interruption, third-party service failures, or consequences of model outputs. This does not exclude or limit liability that cannot be excluded by law.</p>

    <h2>11. Updates</h2>
    <p>OpenDesign may update these Terms. Material changes will be communicated through the page or other reasonable channels. Continued use after changes take effect means you accept the updated terms.</p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Reach us via the <a href="https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design">OpenDesign GitHub repository</a> or the community <a href="https://discord.gg/mHAjSMV6gz">Discord</a>.</p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .legal {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 0 80px;
      color: var(--ink, #262626);
      font-family: var(--sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
      line-height: 1.65;
    }
    .legal-h1 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-family: var(--serif, Georgia, serif);
      font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 44px);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }
    .legal-meta {
      margin: 0 0 28px;
      color: var(--ink-mute, #666);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .legal h2 {
      margin: 32px 0 12px;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.25;
    }
    .legal p,
    .legal li {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .legal ul {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }
    .legal a {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 2px;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
